    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"OMOP Variant Occurrence\"\nexecute:\n  echo: false\n---\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n### Summary\n\nThe **`_variant_occurrence`** table is a custom extension to the OMOP Common Data Model (CDM) that captures detailed genetic variant information identified in patients through genomic testing. This table enables precision oncology research by providing granular variant-level data including genomic coordinates, variant types, molecular consequences, and clinical interpretations.\n\nCurrently, the table contains variants identified via the **Stanford Actionable Mutation Panel for Solid Tumors (STAMP)** test, sourced from the Epic Genomics Suite. STAMP tests processed through Epic Genomics Suite starting in August 2025 are included in this table.\n\n\nEach record in the **`_variant_occurrence`** table includes:\n\n- Genomic information (chromosome, position, DNA/amino acid changes)\n- Variant classification (type, molecular consequence)\n- Clinical interpretation and assessment (tier classification)\n- Test metadata (test name, specimen information)\n- Linkage to clinical context (visit, procedure, provider)\n\nAs of May 2026, this table includes **1,462** patients with **10,347** genetic variants.\n\n\n### Key Considerations\n\n- Only simple variants detected in STAMP tests are present in the source data; fusion variants and copy number variants are not currently reported. We expect that additional variant types will be incorporated in future releases as the dataset continues to evolve.\n\n- The OMOP variant occurrence table does not currently contain Foundation One tests or certain types of variants detected by STAMP (both of which were previously present in the Philips data). We expect that additional STAMP-detected variant types will be available later this year.\n\n\n::: {.columns}\n\n::: {.column width=\"40%\"}\n### 📊 Data Volume \n- **Patient Count:** 1,462\n- **Ordered Tests Count:** 1,571\n- **Variant Count:** 10,347\n:::\n\n::: {.column width=\"60%\"}\n### 🧬 Data Components \n- **Unique Genes:** 331\n- **Molecular Consequences:** 3\n:::\n\n\n## Variant Occurrence Metrics {.tabset}\nThis section presents key metrics and visualizations of genetic variants identified in our patient population through STAMP genomic testing.\nThe following table shows the distribution of patients with variant data across key clinical cohorts:\n\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"datatables html-widget html-fill-item\" id=\"htmlwidget-c5dcc70e4c32332d8d7f\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;\"></div>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"htmlwidget-c5dcc70e4c32332d8d7f\">{\"x\":{\"filter\":\"none\",\"vertical\":false,\"data\":[[\"Total Patients with Variants\",\"Patients with Tumor Board Encounters\",\"Patients with Thoracic Cancer\",\"Patients with Both TB &amp; Thoracic\"],[1462,349,302,110]],\"container\":\"<table class=\\\"display\\\">\\n  <thead>\\n    <tr>\\n      <th>Patient Cohort<\\/th>\\n      <th>Number of Patients<\\/th>\\n    <\\/tr>\\n  <\\/thead>\\n<\\/table>\",\"options\":{\"dom\":\"t\",\"ordering\":false,\"pageLength\":10,\"columnDefs\":[{\"targets\":1,\"render\":\"function(data, type, row, meta) {\\n    return type !== 'display' ? data : DTWidget.formatRound(data, 0, 3, \\\",\\\", \\\".\\\", null);\\n  }\"},{\"className\":\"dt-right\",\"targets\":1},{\"name\":\"Patient Cohort\",\"targets\":0},{\"name\":\"Number of Patients\",\"targets\":1}],\"order\":[],\"autoWidth\":false,\"orderClasses\":false}},\"evals\":[\"options.columnDefs.0.render\"],\"jsHooks\":[]}</script>\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n\n\n**Note:** Tumor board patients are identified by visit records containing \"tumor board\" (case-insensitive). Thoracic cancer patients are identified from NeuralFrame diagnoses with primary sites including lung, bronchus, or thymus. \n\n\n\n\n### Genomic Testing Timeline\n\nThe following visualization shows the monthly trend of genomic test orders over time with cumulative totals.\n\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"plotly html-widget html-fill-item\" id=\"htmlwidget-2334c7eec280188d6eb1\" style=\"width:100%;height:390px;\"></div>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"htmlwidget-2334c7eec280188d6eb1\">{\"x\":{\"visdat\":{\"82b71365d430\":[\"function () \",\"plotlyVisDat\"]},\"cur_data\":\"82b71365d430\",\"attrs\":{\"82b71365d430\":{\"alpha_stroke\":1,\"sizes\":[10,100],\"spans\":[1,20],\"x\":{},\"y\":{},\"type\":\"bar\",\"name\":\"Monthly Tests\",\"marker\":{\"color\":\"#8dd3c7\",\"opacity\":0.69999999999999996},\"hovertemplate\":\"<b>%{x|%B %Y}<\\/b><br> Monthly Tests: %{y:,.0f}<br> <extra><\\/extra>\",\"inherit\":true},\"82b71365d430.1\":{\"alpha_stroke\":1,\"sizes\":[10,100],\"spans\":[1,20],\"x\":{},\"y\":{},\"type\":\"scatter\",\"mode\":\"lines\",\"yaxis\":\"y2\",\"name\":\"Cumulative Tests\",\"line\":{\"color\":\"#fb8072\",\"width\":3},\"marker\":{\"size\":8,\"color\":\"#fb8072\"},\"hovertemplate\":\"<b>%{x|%B %Y}<\\/b><br> Total Tests: %{y:,.0f}<br> <extra><\\/extra>\",\"inherit\":true}},\"layout\":{\"margin\":{\"b\":100,\"l\":60,\"t\":25,\"r\":80},\"xaxis\":{\"domain\":[0,1],\"automargin\":true,\"title\":\"\"},\"yaxis\":{\"domain\":[0,1],\"automargin\":true,\"title\":\"Monthly Test Volume\",\"titlefont\":{\"color\":\"#8dd3c7\"},\"tickfont\":{\"color\":\"#8dd3c7\"}},\"yaxis2\":{\"title\":\"Cumulative Tests\",\"titlefont\":{\"color\":\"#fb8072\"},\"tickfont\":{\"color\":\"#fb8072\"},\"overlaying\":\"y\",\"side\":\"right\"},\"title\":\"\",\"hovermode\":\"x unified\",\"legend\":{\"orientation\":\"h\",\"x\":0.5,\"xanchor\":\"center\",\"y\":-0.14999999999999999},\"showlegend\":true},\"source\":\"A\",\"config\":{\"modeBarButtonsToAdd\":[\"hoverclosest\",\"hovercompare\"],\"showSendToCloud\":false},\"data\":[{\"x\":[\"2025-09-01\",\"2025-10-01\",\"2025-11-01\",\"2025-12-01\",\"2026-01-01\",\"2026-02-01\",\"2026-03-01\",\"2026-04-01\"],\"y\":[26,171,123,168,158,367,45